## Configuration

You can configure {{displayName}} through the SimpleNS Admin Dashboard or declaratively in your `simplens.config.yaml`.

```yaml
providers:
  - name: {{name}}
    package: '@simplens/plugin-{{name}}'
    credentials:
{{#each credentials}}
      {{this}}: ${{screamingSnakeCase this}}
{{/each}}
{{#unless credentials.length}}
      # Add your credentials here
{{/unless}}
    options:
      rateLimit:
        maxTokens: 100
        refillRate: 10
        refillInterval: second
      # Optional file attachment limit overrides (omit to use plugin defaults)
      ATTACHMENT_MAX_FILE_SIZE: '25MB'
      ATTACHMENT_MAX_COUNT: 10
      ATTACHMENT_ALLOWED_MIME_TYPES:
        - application/pdf
        - image/jpeg
        - image/png
        - text/plain
```

---

## File Attachment Support

This plugin declares baseline attachment limits in its manifest. Administrators can adjust these limits per provider instance in the SimpleNS Dashboard or via provider `options`.

### Manifest Defaults

| Parameter | Default Value | Description |
|:---|:---|:---|
| `enabled` | `true` | Whether file attachments are supported |
| `maxFileSize` | `10MB` (`10485760` bytes) | Baseline maximum size per attached file |
| `maxCount` | `5` | Maximum number of attachments per notification |
| `allowedMimeTypes` | `pdf, txt, csv, jpeg, png, webp` | Allowed MIME types / patterns |

### Dynamic Runtime Overrides

You can override these limits per provider tier using standard optional config keys:

- `ATTACHMENT_MAX_FILE_SIZE`: String (e.g. `'25MB'`, `'500KB'`) or numeric bytes (`26214400`).
- `ATTACHMENT_MAX_COUNT`: Integer limit (e.g. `10`).
- `ATTACHMENT_ALLOWED_MIME_TYPES`: Array of MIME types or wildcards (e.g. `['image/*', 'application/pdf']`).
- `ATTACHMENT_ENABLED`: Boolean (`true` / `false`).

When omitted, the provider automatically falls back to manifest baseline limits.

